                                                "sense_id": "b1753af2-3474-3cc0-bb22-4d1e1c1434ed",
                                                "text": "[Joseph Black's] experiments on magnesia alba, quick lime, and other alkaline substances proved that \"fixed air\" is given off when limestone is burned, and that the same loss is incurred when it is dissolved in muriatic acid (hydrochloric acid)."
